-- S89 Visual Inventory Intelligence: data foundation (WP1) and the SQL twin of
-- supabase/functions/_shared/product-identity.mjs (WP2).
--
-- Owner gate (binding, 2026-09-24):
--   * Stored names, aliases and identity keys keep every letter. Icelandic
--     Á á Ð ð É é Í í Ó ó Ú ú Ý ý Þ þ Æ æ Ö ö are case-folded, never
--     transliterated. Accent-insensitive and bilingual matching exists only as
--     search keys in atlas_private.inventory_search_documents (derived,
--     rebuildable) and is never written back to items or aliases.
--   * No automatic backfill of canonical inventory data. This migration writes
--     no inventory_items row and changes no existing alias value. The new item
--     attribute columns start empty; suggestions for them go through the
--     catalog approval queue (S89 governance migration). The derived key and
--     search tables below are indexes over existing rows, not canonical data.
--   * pg_trgm is NOT created here. Trigram search is used only when the
--     extension is already installed (guarded, dynamic SQL); the default path
--     is PostgreSQL full-text + token matching. Enabling pg_trgm is a rollout
--     approval item: after approval run
--       create extension if not exists pg_trgm with schema extensions;
--       select atlas_private.inventory_search_enable_trigram();
--   * Recognition can never write quantities: every atlas_recognition_* body
--     runs as the NOLOGIN role atlas_recognition_definer, which has no write
--     grant on any quantity-bearing table and no execute on any writer.
--
-- Contents:
--   1. product identity functions (fold, search fold, tokens, keys, package
--      parser, code normaliser, duplicate score) - parity-tested with the JS
--   2. item attribute columns (empty), taxonomy reference table
--   3. derived identity keys with a unique active identity (pre-flight abort)
--   4. codes table (new codes only) + a read-through lookup over legacy columns
--   5. alias governance columns (existing rows untouched) + unique approved key
--   6. derived search documents (FTS default, trigram when installed)
--   7. recognition audit tables, ai_media purpose and retention reason
--   8. scanner live-apply permanently disabled
--   9. the recognition definer role, grants, policies and its read/record RPCs
--
-- Service-role-only public wrappers follow the S88 pattern: invoker wrappers,
-- execute granted to service_role only, the database re-checks the actor.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. Product identity functions
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Constants generated by `node scripts/product_identity_constants.mjs`; the
-- Node parity test fails when they differ from the shared JS module.
create or replace function atlas_private.product_identity_constants()
returns jsonb
language sql
immutable
parallel safe
